# Project Reference: DataSite Impact Analyzer

**Single source of truth:** All docs and AI rules must stay aligned. Use these as the canonical set:

- **`projectspec.md`** — Full API schemas, data sources (§3), calculation formulas, ML training, pre-hackathon checklist.
- **`AGENTS.md`** — Required proposal inputs, optional PDF ingestor, data-source URLs, practical rules.
- **`projectoverview.md`** — Pitch, user flow, judging criteria, target award (Google Best Sustainability AI Hack).
- **`README.md`** — Quickstart, backend scripts, branching.

This rule summarizes the product and points the AI to the right contracts.

---

## What We're Building

**DataSite Impact Analyzer** — A web app for **city councils and urban planners** to input a proposed data centre’s technical parameters and a Canadian location, then receive a **scored multi-dimensional impact report** (environmental, economic, sociological) powered by **real Canadian open data** and a trained **XGBoost ML model**.

**Pitch for demo:** Canada is investing in sovereign AI compute. Poorly sited projects face community pushback and regulatory delays. This tool helps get siting right before the first shovel goes in.

**Hackathon:** GenAI Genesis 2026 | Google Sustainability Track. **Minimize features, maximize real data.**

---

## Three AI Techniques (Tell Judges All Three)

1. **Deterministic calculation engine** — Real formulas from published benchmarks (IEA, The Green Grid WUE, CBRE, etc.) applied to real Canadian datasets.
2. **XGBoost ML model** — Trained on real IESO/AESO historical grid data to predict **grid strain probability** from a proposed load addition.
3. **Groq LLM** — Grounded report + negotiation playbook generation; it may **only cite numbers** produced by layers 1 and 2 (no invented figures).

---

## Tech Stack

- **Frontend:** TypeScript, Next.js 16.1.6, Tailwind v4, **pnpm 10.32.1** (use pnpm only, not npm).
- **Backend:** Python 3.14, FastAPI 0.135, uv 0.10.10.
- **ML:** scikit-learn + XGBoost (trained offline, loaded at runtime).
- **Geo:** MapTiler API (geocoding, map tiles, land cover).
- **LLM:** Groq API (e.g. llama-3.3-70b-versatile or mixtral-8x7b).
- **Data:** Electricity Maps, IESO/AESO, StatsCan, Indigenous Services Canada, ECCC drought; see full spec for URLs and fallbacks.

